From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: implement 3GPP USSD over the CS path

The plugin had no org.freedesktop.ModemManager1.Modem.Modem3gpp.Ussd
interface at all, so a `mmcli --3gpp-ussd-initiate` was refused and a
network-initiated notification was dropped on the floor.

The CP's three messages are SEND_USSD (0x0505), CANCEL_USSD (0x0506) and the
ON_USSD (0x0510) indication. A request is `[u8 flag][u8 dcs][packed GSM
septets]` in a fixed 185-byte field, which is how the vendor library builds
it; a cancel is the header alone. The indication's first word is the RIL
mode -- 0 NOTIFY, 1 REQUEST, 2 NW_RELEASE, 3 LOCAL_CLIENT, 4 NOT_SUPPORTED,
5 NW_TIMEOUT -- in the u32 slot a response would use for its status.

This goes over CS even with IMS up. Stock's logcat for a dialled code says
`isUt=true useImsForUt=false` and then "Sending ussd string over CS pipe",
and the AIMS USSD request never appears in a capture on this carrier
config, so Ut/XCAP is not in the path here. `*#21#` and friends are MMI
codes the dialer turns into a call-forwarding interrogation (0x0d14), not
USSD, which is why they answer while a real code does not.

The interface's unsolicited-event vfuncs are set to no-ops rather than left
alone: ON_USSD arrives on the control port that is already dispatched, and
mm-iface-modem-3gpp-ussd.c calls those four without a NULL guard, so what
we would otherwise inherit from MMBroadbandModem is the AT `+CUSD` path on
a modem with no AT port.

The reply text layout is inferred and marked as such in the code. Every
code tried against both SIMs on this account answered mode 4 with the whole
field zeroed, so only the mode has been seen for real; the text is read as
`[u8 dcs][packed septets]` to mirror the request, which is what the vendor
library's DecodingUssd(dcs, ...) pairing implies, and the raw bytes are
logged so the first network that answers settles it.
diff -ruN a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.c b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.c
